# Dregg-180 v2 floorplan: Metal5 over the register file is reserved for the tamper shield.
# Sourced after rf_array.tcl. Signal routing is kept off Metal5 above the array band (the array's own
# wiring needs Metal1 to Metal4 only: word lines on Metal3, bit lines on Metal2/Metal4), so that a
# serpentine driven and checked by the canary logic can be drawn there between the Metal5 supply
# straps. This file makes the reservation that the routing experiments run against; the serpentine
# itself is generated by tools/gen_shield.py once the RTL has a shield net with two named pins.
lassign $::rf_band ya yb
set m5 [[ord::get_db_tech] findLayer Metal5]
set core [$::block getCoreArea]
odb::dbObstruction_create $::block $m5 [$core xMin] [expr {int($ya * $::dbu)}] [$core xMax] [expr {int($yb * $::dbu)}]
metric shield_m5_reserved_um2 [format %.0f [expr {([$core xMax] - [$core xMin]) / double($::dbu) * ($yb - $ya)}]]
